ml-slop — code skill (formerly the code-density-analyzer plugin)
=================================================================

Authored by Max Levitskiy and distributed under the MIT License (see LICENSE).

Adapts the methodology of the text skill (formerly text-density-analyzer) — parallel analysis
subagents feeding a weighted composite score, validated against human-edited
references — from prose to code. The ten code-analysis methods are new; five
inherit the prompt patterns of their text-density counterparts (duplication ←
claim-similarity, dead code ← filler, comment redundancy ← new-information,
verbosity ← compression-ratio, boilerplate ← structure-template) and five are
code-specific (over-abstraction, error-masking, convention-adherence,
hallucinated-deps, perf-waste).

The text skill was originally authored by Web-Tree
(https://github.com/Web-tree) and ships in the same ml-slop plugin.
